From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:09:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/40] Metal diamond engine: Debye materials on the GPU
 (snapshot cg23)

Engine_Ext_DebyeMaterial (exactly that class) runs per tile on the GPU: Pre (pole
states from V^n) in the Pre stage with Mur and Drude/Lorentz, Post (the implicit
solve from V_raw, the correction, the pole states finished) in the Post stage with
Mur, after the UPML Post stage; Apply (V -= correction) in the extension-order Apply
list. Arithmetic as clang contracts the CPU code (W = fma(v_relax, W_old, v_drive*V),
W += v_drive*V one fmadd). The dispersive element records now carry their own
coefficient and state offsets (Debye: 6P+3 coefficients, 6+3P state floats).

emsKit diamond_check.sh 54 of 54 (new: a two-pole Debye block on a Mur box, and in the
case with PML, Mur, lumped RLC, Drude/Lorentz and conducting sheets); debye_check.sh
passes. The CPU code changes only by friend declarations.

